BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Femmemoir: A zine-making workshop
DTSTART:20261017T130000
DTEND:20261017T130000
UID:1416c765e322ef46e224e12d6e660f24@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Led by the curators of the On Our Own Terms exhibition\, this 
 workshop offers the chance to explore zine-making as a medium for memoir a
 nd queer history. Zine-making experienced a renaissance in the 90s – the
  last analogue decade – and was strongly linked to DIY feminist and quee
 r activism\, including the queercore and riot grrrl movements. Come and le
 arn more about the history of queer zines and create your own “femmemoir
 ” – a mini personal and cultural archive. All materials will be provid
 ed. ‍
LOCATION:The ArQuives\, 34 Isabella Street
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/femmemoir-a-zine-making-workshop
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
