BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DJ HEATHER b2b COLETTE [All Night Long]
DTSTART:20261017T220000
DTEND:20261017T220000
UID:5ec17a14fff8f4e2a864ee75fd28e9a9@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Sat Oct 17: DJ HEATHER b2b COLETTE Opening beats by: Mr Haze ~
 ~ TICKETS ~~ HOUSE OF OM 20TH ANNIVERSARY: COLETTE B2B DJ HEATHER The 20th
  anniversary of the iconic House of OM: Colette &amp\; DJ Heather compilat
 ion marks a milestone for two pioneers of the electronic music scene. Rele
 ased in June 2006 on OM Records\, this double-disc mix became a definitive
  moment for Chicago house music\, spotlighting the lifelong friendship and
  musical synergy of two of the genre’s most formidable talents. Before t
 hey became global headliners\, Colette and DJ Heather forged their bond in
  the fertile underground of 1990s Chicago\, driven by a shared love for th
 e city’s signature four-on-the-floor sound. By the mid-2000s\, both arti
 sts had been signed to San Francisco’s powerhouse label\, OM Records\, e
 stablishing themselves as heavy hitters who performed hundreds of shows an
 nually. This culminated in the release of House of OM: Colette &amp\; DJ H
 eather. The double-album perfectly captured their complementary sonic iden
 tities: Disc 1 (Colette) sparkled with smooth\, funky\, vocal-heavy tracks
 \, featuring her own performance on “All The Same” alongside contribut
 ions from Kaskade\, Andy Caldwell\, and Greenskeepers. Disc 2 (DJ Heather)
  delivered a deeper\, instrumental-focused exploration of Chicago jack\, f
 eaturing tracks from Inland Knights\, Giom\, and Mark Farina. The release 
 was an instant underground and commercial favourite within the dance commu
 nity\, serving as a masterclass in track selection and seamless mixing. Fo
 llowing the release\, the duo embarked on extensive North American tours w
 ith fellow OM label mates. The success of those shows laid the groundwork 
 for their annual Second City Sessions tours\, launched in 2009. This colla
 borative banner featured Colette and DJ Heather playing extended back-to-b
 ack sets\, a tradition that has earned a massive\, dedicated following ove
 r the decades. Reflecting on their long personal friendship and the 20-yea
